cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  The conditional value of AI in supply-chain demand planning: a reproducible
  out-of-sample benchmark across the intermittency spectrum
message: If you use this code or these results, please cite the work.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Patel
    given-names: Nishchay
repository-code: https://github.com/NISHCHAY026/ai-demand-planning-benchmark
license: MIT
keywords:
  - demand forecasting
  - intermittent demand
  - supply chain
  - machine learning
  - gradient boosting
  - deep learning
  - out-of-sample evaluation
  - M5
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Benchmarks classical statistical forecasters (Naive, moving average, simple
  exponential smoothing, Croston, Syntetos-Boylan), a global gradient-boosted
  model (LightGBM), and two deep global neural forecasters (NHITS, DeepAR) on
  two public retail datasets under one identical rolling-origin out-of-sample
  protocol. Reports that in-sample method selection inverts out-of-sample, that
  the value of machine-learning forecasters is conditional on demand regime and
  data sufficiency, and documents a same-week transacted-price target leak that
  inflates apparent model accuracy on transactional data.
